    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-03-28T09:14:46Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hi!\r\n\r\nThe 'mini.sessions' module uses [built-in sessions](https://neovim.io/doc/user/usr_21.html#21.4). What is saved there is controlled by ['sessionoptions'](https://neovim.io/doc/user/options.html#'sessionoptions') option, which only has a flag for saving global variables. So Neovim's session would be a reason for not saving tab-local variables.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The 'mini.sessions' module uses <a href=\"https://neovim.io/doc/user/usr_21.html#21.4\" rel=\"nofollow\">built-in sessions</a>. What is saved there is controlled by <a href=\"https://neovim.io/doc/user/options.html#'sessionoptions'\" rel=\"nofollow\">'sessionoptions'</a> option, which only has a flag for saving global variables. So Neovim's session would be a reason for not saving tab-local variables.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Hi!\nThe 'mini.sessions' module uses built-in sessions. What is saved there is controlled by 'sessionoptions' option, which only has a flag for saving global variables. So Neovim's session would be a reason for not saving tab-local variables.",
